## How GitHub Was Used

The team continued working in the Phase 1 EchoEats GitHub repository for Sprint 2. Each of the six members contributed from their own GitHub account and worked on a separate feature branch named after their deliverable (for example `sprint2/class-diagram`), so work could proceed in parallel without overwriting anyone else's files. Members committed regularly during the sprint with descriptive messages, which gives a dated version history of each design document and lets earlier versions be restored if needed. When a deliverable was ready, its owner opened a pull request into `main`. Other members reviewed the pull requests and left comments on correctness, consistency with the Phase 1 requirements and alignment with the other diagrams. Changes were merged after review. This workflow gave version control, peer review and a traceable record of each member's contribution, and the links in the table above point to that evidence.
